## Evidence Type

Retrospective Testimony

## Witness

Carlos Mora

## Recorded

2026-08-22

## Subject

Origin of the Forge–Stage Method

## Evidentiary Boundary

This testimony was recorded retrospectively on 2026-08-22.

It describes events that occurred before the earliest surviving
documentary record presently available.

It is not contemporaneous evidence of those events and SHALL NOT
be represented as such.

## Testimony

As you are already aware, it all started with trying to get the
BLTouch to work on the CR-10S printer. After many attempts at
changing settings, we started losing track of what we were doing,
so we came up with a method that only changed one thing at a time
and saved the evidence.

From there, we decided it should be more formal. Hence,
The Stage Method was born.

During our initial documentation, we found that we needed to ask
many questions. Then the Forge was born.

The Forge helped us answer the questions, and the Anvil
(The Stage Method) became the verifier.

From there it started to grow into a methodology, which I coined
the term the Forge-Stage Method.

It became an implementation as it grew while we were still
investigating the BLTouch on the CR-10S.
